{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01FoieFdePiP8gUbJba9otah","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to generate detailed imagined experiment results for the \"worst\" tier scenario across all planned experiments in the experiment plan. I need to carefully consider what \"worst\" means based on the definition provided and generate realistic but pessimistic results for each experiment.\n\nLet me go through each planned experiment and generate worst-case (but still plausible) results with rationales.\n\nKey worst-tier characteristics:\n- Core numerical claims weakened by robustness checks\n- GDN confound is fatal\n- Equalizer paradox novelty insufficient standalone\n- Need reframe angle\n- Specific metric ranges provided\n\n\nNow I'm working through the nine non-cancelled experiments systematically, generating worst-case results for each one that align with the metric ranges and narrative constraints provided.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10818,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10818},"output_tokens":22,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9ac07f93-f2d8-47a3-aa19-d12650caf590","uuid":"35607dc9-a040-4087-b683-2b261bb7e3bc"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01FoieFdePiP8gUbJba9otah","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntier: worst\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  原始三条 claim 均无法以当前强度成立。Reframe 策略（仍冲 EMNLP，不降级）：放弃 \"equalizer effect\" 作为核心贡献，\n  转向 per-example analysis methodology paper。新 angle: \"Per-Example Probing Reveals Hidden Heterogeneity\n  in Hybrid Architecture Evaluations\"——核心论点变为：aggregate benchmark 评估掩盖了架构间的 per-example 行为差异，\n  即使 aggregate 指标相近，底层机制完全不同。这是 methodology + cautionary tale 的 framing：(1) 提出\n  per-example divergence metrics (Jaccard, net-effect asymmetry) 作为评估工具，(2) 用 Wang et al. model zoo\n  做 case study 展示 aggregate metric 的盲区，(3) 给出 practitioner recommendation——选架构时不能只看\n  leaderboard 数字。即使 equalizer effect 本身不 robust，per-example heterogeneity 的存在及其对架构选择的\n  implication 仍是 solid contribution。标题: \"Beyond Aggregate Benchmarks: Per-Example Analysis Exposes\n  Architecture-Specific Behavior in Hybrid Language Models\"。投 EMNLP Findings。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"Task-specificity characterization of equalizer effect\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-001\"\n    description: >\n      对 6 个 benchmark 计算各 attention ratio 下 cross-architecture std，构建连续 retrieval demand 谱。\n    expected_results:\n      lambada_rho: -0.60\n      lambada_rho_permutation_p: 0.117\n      lambada_std_reduction_pct: 38\n      arc_easy_rho: -0.30\n      arc_easy_p: 0.35\n      arc_challenge_rho: -0.10\n      hellaswag_rho: 0.05\n      winogrande_rho: 0.15\n      mmlu_rho: -0.20\n      benchmarks_with_rho_below_neg05: 1\n      dose_response_r_squared: 0.28\n    result_rationale: >\n      排除 GDN 后 LAMBADA ρ 从 -1.0 退化至约 -0.6（RetNet 和 HGRN2 的 h24 点 std 回弹导致非单调），\n      permutation p 跃升至 0.117 不再显著。核心原因：D004 confound——GDN 在高 attention ratio 配置下\n      使用了不同的 normalization scheme，其 std 被人为压低，移除后整体 convergence 幅度大打折扣。\n      ARC-Easy ρ 仅 -0.3，其余 benchmark 无趋势。连续 retrieval demand 谱的 R² 仅 0.28，\n      WinoGrande 作为含 retrieval 成分的 coreference task 却 ρ=+0.15，直接破坏 dose-response 叙事。\n      无法建立\"retrieval demand 调制 convergence strength\"的 principled taxonomy。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 1: Cross-architecture std reduction and Spearman ρ by benchmark (1.3B, GDN excluded)\"\n        columns: [benchmark, retrieval_demand_score, std_at_h0, std_at_h24, reduction_pct, spearman_rho, permutation_p]\n        rows:\n          - [LAMBADA, 0.90, 0.024, 0.015, 38, -0.60, 0.117]\n          - [ARC-Easy, 0.55, 0.031, 0.025, 19, -0.30, 0.350]\n          - [ARC-Challenge, 0.50, 0.028, 0.026, 7, -0.10, 0.680]\n          - [HellaSwag, 0.30, 0.019, 0.019, 0, 0.05, 0.920]\n          - [WinoGrande, 0.45, 0.022, 0.025, -14, 0.15, 0.610]\n          - [MMLU, 0.35, 0.035, 0.031, 11, -0.20, 0.480]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 1: 6-panel plot of cross-arch std vs attention ratio。LAMBADA 面板显示含/不含 GDN 两条线——含 GDN 时呈现漂亮的单调下降，排除 GDN 后 h24 处 rebound 明显，非单调。其余 5 个 benchmark 基本 flat 或 noisy。\"\n      - \"Fig 2: Dose-response scatter (retrieval demand score vs ρ)，6 点，R²=0.28，WinoGrande 为明显 outlier 位于右上方。虚线为线性 fit，95% CI 极宽。\"\n    analysis: >\n      task-specificity 叙事崩溃。GDN 排除后 LAMBADA 自身不再显著，dose-response 因 WinoGrande outlier\n      R² 仅 0.28。Claim 1 无法以\"retrieval demand 调制 convergence\"的形式成立。但 per-example 异质性\n      本身仍存在——reframe 方向：不再声称 convergence 是 systematic phenomenon，而是用这些负结果作为\n      evidence 说明 aggregate metric 不可靠。\n\n  - name: \"Multi-benchmark per-example analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-002\"\n    description: >\n      对 HellaSwag、ARC-Easy、ARC-Challenge 收集 1.3B 和 340M 的 per-example logprob 数据，\n      分析非 LAMBADA 任务的 per-example convergence 行为。\n    expected_results:\n      hellaswag_per_example_convergence: \"absent — random reshuffling\"\n      arc_easy_rho_per_example: -0.15\n      arc_easy_per_example_pattern: \"weak convergence in a ~12% subset, rest noise\"\n      arc_challenge_rho_per_example: 0.05\n      arc_challenge_per_example_pattern: \"no detectable structure\"\n      fraction_samples_with_consistent_direction: 0.18\n      cross_benchmark_jaccard_convergent_samples: 0.04\n    result_rationale: >\n      非 LAMBADA 任务本身 aggregate convergence 就不存在或极弱（exp-001 已示），per-example 分析\n      进一步暴露问题：ARC-Easy 的 per-example 分析反而显示大部分 sample 上 attention 的 effect 方向\n      在不同 architecture 间不一致，只有约 12% 的 easy retrieval-type 题目呈现弱 convergence，\n      但该 subset 太小无法支撑 claim。HellaSwag per-example 完全无结构——helped/hurt set 在不同\n      attention ratio 间剧烈变动，bootstrap stability <0.3。ARC-Challenge 类似。\n      这直接破坏了 \"task-specificity\" 叙事：原本期望非 LAMBADA 任务 per-example 也无 convergence\n      （从而 confirm aggregate 结果），但实际是 per-example 呈现 weak, inconsistent convergence 信号，\n      既无法说 \"converging\" 也无法干净地说 \"not converging\"，而是 noisy mess，削弱了\n      LAMBADA 作为 clean contrast 的地位。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 2: Per-example convergence metrics across benchmarks (1.3B)\"\n        columns: [benchmark, n_samples, frac_consistent_direction, per_example_rho, bootstrap_stability, interpretation]\n        rows:\n          - [LAMBADA, 5153, 0.61, -0.55, 0.78, \"moderate convergence (weakened vs aggregate)\"]\n          - [ARC-Easy, 2376, 0.23, -0.15, 0.41, \"weak, noisy — small convergent subset\"]\n          - [ARC-Challenge, 1172, 0.15, 0.05, 0.22, \"no structure\"]\n          - [HellaSwag, 10042, 0.12, 0.02, 0.18, \"no structure — random reshuffling\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 3: Per-example effect heatmap (sample × attention ratio) for 4 benchmarks。LAMBADA 显示一定的 block structure（某些 sample 一致 helped/hurt），但 block 边界模糊。ARC-Easy 有零星 cluster。HellaSwag 和 ARC-Challenge 基本纯噪声。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Per-example 分析未能干净地 validate task-specificity。LAMBADA per-example ρ 从 aggregate 的 -0.6\n      进一步弱化至 -0.55（因为 per-example level 噪声更大），而非 LAMBADA 任务并非 \"cleanly absent\"\n      而是 \"noisy and inconclusive\"。这意味着无法构建 \"LAMBADA converges, others don't\" 的 clean binary。\n      但 per-example heterogeneity 本身（不同 architecture 在相同 sample 上行为不同）在所有 benchmark\n      上都存在——这支持 reframed methodology paper 的核心论点。\n\n  - name: \"Helped/hurt sample characterization\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-003\"\n    description: >\n      对 LAMBADA 的 helped/hurt sample 计算 token frequency、context length、perplexity、\n      topic distribution，测试是否有可解释的 feature 区分。\n    expected_results:\n      best_feature_p_value: 0.034\n      best_feature_name: \"target_token_log_frequency\"\n      best_feature_effect_size_cohens_d: 0.18\n      context_length_p: 0.22\n      perplexity_p: 0.41\n      topic_chi2_p: 0.15\n      cross_architecture_feature_difference: \"not significant after Bonferroni\"\n      sample_feature_best_p: 0.034\n    result_rationale: >\n      无 feature 通过 Bonferroni 校正后的 p<0.01 阈值。最佳 single feature (target token frequency)\n      raw p=0.034 但校正后 p≈0.14（4 features × 3 architectures = 12 comparisons）。\n      effect size Cohen's d=0.18 极小。核心问题：helped/hurt sample 的区分不在简单的 surface feature 上，\n      而可能在更高阶的 distributional property 中，但我们没有足够的 feature engineering 来捕捉。\n      Cross-architecture comparison 更惨：三个 architecture 的 helped sample 在所有 feature 上的\n      分布无显著差异，意味着无法给出 \"GDN helps long-context samples while HGRN2 helps rare-token samples\"\n      这类 interpretable story。Claim 3 的 mechanistic depth 严重不足。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 3: Feature comparison of helped vs hurt samples on LAMBADA (per architecture)\"\n        columns: [feature, architecture, helped_mean, hurt_mean, cohens_d, raw_p, bonferroni_p]\n        rows:\n          - [target_token_log_freq, GDN, 8.21, 8.45, 0.18, 0.034, 0.41]\n          - [target_token_log_freq, RetNet, 8.18, 8.39, 0.15, 0.065, 0.78]\n          - [target_token_log_freq, HGRN2, 8.30, 8.42, 0.09, 0.210, 1.00]\n          - [context_length, GDN, 42.3, 40.8, 0.08, 0.220, 1.00]\n          - [context_length, RetNet, 43.1, 41.5, 0.10, 0.180, 1.00]\n          - [context_length, HGRN2, 41.8, 41.2, 0.04, 0.550, 1.00]\n          - [baseline_perplexity, GDN, 12.4, 11.8, 0.07, 0.410, 1.00]\n          - [baseline_perplexity, RetNet, 13.1, 12.5, 0.06, 0.480, 1.00]\n          - [baseline_perplexity, HGRN2, 12.0, 11.9, 0.01, 0.870, 1.00]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 4: Violin plot of target token log-frequency for helped vs hurt samples，三个 architecture 分 panel。分布高度重叠，几乎不可区分。\"\n      - \"Fig 5: 2D t-SNE of sample feature vectors，colored by helped/hurt。无可见 cluster 分离。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Sample characterization 失败——无可解释结构。这对原始 Claim 3 是致命的：我们说 \"attention acts on\n      different samples per architecture\" 但无法解释 why。对 reframed paper 影响较小：methodology paper\n      可以将此作为 open question (\"per-example heterogeneity exists but its drivers remain unclear,\n      motivating future work on finer-grained sample characterization\")。\n\n  - name: \"Attention weight extraction and visualization\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-004\"\n    description: >\n      提取 h3-1 配置下三个 architecture 的 attention weight pattern，分析与 per-example effect 的相关性。\n    expected_results:\n      attention_per_example_correlation_gdn: 0.11\n      attention_per_example_correlation_retnet: 0.08\n      attention_per_example_correlation_hgrn2: 0.14\n      attention_per_example_correlation_mean: 0.11\n      cross_arch_attention_similarity: 0.35\n      attention_entropy_helped_vs_hurt_p: 0.18\n    result_rationale: >\n      Attention pattern 与 per-example effect 的相关性极低（mean r=0.11，远低于 pass criterion 0.3）。\n      原因：h3-1 配置中 attention 只有 1 层（共 24 层中），大量信息处理发生在 recurrence layers 中，\n      单层 attention 的 weight pattern 不足以解释 per-example 行为差异。attention entropy 在\n      helped vs hurt samples 间也无显著差异（p=0.18）。cross-architecture attention similarity 0.35\n      表明不同 architecture 的 attention layer 确实关注不同 position，但这与 per-example outcome 无法\n      建立因果链。没有 mechanistic story。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 4: Attention pattern analysis (h3-1, 1.3B)\"\n        columns: [architecture, attn_per_example_corr, attn_entropy_mean, entropy_helped_vs_hurt_p, cross_arch_cosine_sim]\n        rows:\n          - [GDN, 0.11, 3.42, 0.22, \"-\"]\n          - [RetNet, 0.08, 3.18, 0.31, \"0.35 (vs GDN)\"]\n          - [HGRN2, 0.14, 3.55, 0.14, \"0.32 (vs GDN)\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 6: Attention heatmap for 10 representative LAMBADA samples across 3 architectures。视觉上 pattern 不同（GDN 集中在末尾 token，RetNet 更 distributed，HGRN2 有双峰），但这些差异与 helped/hurt 无对应关系。\"\n      - \"Fig 7: Scatter of attention-based prediction score vs actual per-example effect。三个 panel 均为散点云，r<0.15。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Mechanistic analysis 失败。无法从 attention weights 解释 per-example divergence。这对 Claim 3\n      \"complementary mechanisms\" 是毁灭性的——我们无法说明 mechanisms 是什么。对 reframed paper：\n      methodology paper 不需要 explain 机制，只需 demonstrate 现象存在。attention 可视化仍可作为\n      qualitative illustration 放在 appendix，但不再是 core evidence。\n\n  - name: \"Architecture expansion check\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-005\"\n    description: >\n      搜索 Wang et al. model zoo 及其他来源，寻找 GDN/RetNet/HGRN2 之外的 hybrid architectures。\n    expected_results:\n      additional_architectures_found: 0\n      wang_et_al_architectures_total: 3\n      mamba_hybrid_available: false\n      rwkv_hybrid_available: false\n      architectures_tested: 3\n    result_rationale: >\n      Wang et al. (2507.06457) 的 model zoo 明确仅包含 GDN、RetNet、HGRN2 三种 architecture。\n      搜索 HuggingFace 和其他公开 model zoo 后未发现使用相同 training setup（相同数据、相同 token 数、\n      相同超参搜索）的其他 hybrid architecture checkpoint。Mamba-2 hybrid 存在于 Zamba 等项目中但\n      training setup 完全不同，apple-to-apple comparison 不可能。n=3 limitation 无法缓解。\n      这对原始 Claim 1 的 generalizability 和 reframed paper 都是问题——reviewer 会质疑\n      findings 是否只是这 3 个特定 architecture 的 artifact。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Architecture expansion 失败，n=3 limitation 确认。Reframed paper 需要在 Limitations 中\n      prominently 承认，并 argue 3 architectures 代表 3 种不同 recurrence mechanism（这是 Wang et al.\n      的选择 rationale），同时将 generalization 作为 future work。\n\n  - name: \"340M rebound mechanism analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-007\"\n    description: >\n      深入分析 340M 在 attn=8 处的非单调 rebound，对比 1.3B 同 attention ratio 的 per-example 行为。\n    expected_results:\n      rebound_mechanism_identified: false\n      scale_340m_rebound_magnitude: 0.018\n      scale_1_3b_at_same_ratio_std: 0.007\n      per_example_overlap_340m_1_3b: 0.22\n      training_tokens_confound_resolved: false\n      explanation_confidence: \"low\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      340M rebound 无法解释。Per-example 对比显示 340M 和 1.3B 在 attn=8 ratio 上 affected sample\n      overlap 仅 0.22（低但非零），暗示 scale 和 attention 以不可分离的方式交互。更严重的是，\n      340M 训练了 20B tokens vs 1.3B 训练了 100B tokens（Wang et al. setup），training token count\n      与 model scale 完全 confounded，无法归因 rebound 到 \"insufficient model capacity\" vs\n      \"insufficient training\"。这使 Claim 2 退化为纯粹的 unexplained observation：我们看到\n      340M 和 1.3B 行为不同，但无法说 why。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 5: 340M vs 1.3B per-example comparison at attn=8\"\n        columns: [metric, \"340M\", \"1.3B\", delta]\n        rows:\n          - [cross_arch_std, 0.018, 0.007, \"+0.011\"]\n          - [per_example_overlap_jaccard, \"-\", \"-\", 0.22]\n          - [rebound_samples_frac, 0.31, 0.08, \"+0.23\"]\n          - [training_tokens_B, 20, 100, \"confounded\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 8: 340M vs 1.3B cross-arch std trajectory。1.3B 单调下降（GDN excluded 后变为 weakly 下降），340M 在 h8 处 rebound。两条线 diverge 但 error bars 在 h8 处 overlap。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Claim 2 (scale-dependent convergence) 退化为 unexplained observation。Training token confound\n      无法解开。Reframed paper 处理方式：将 scale contrast 作为一个 observation 报告（不作为 claim），\n      在 Discussion 中 acknowledge training token confound，frame as \"preliminary evidence that\n      per-example heterogeneity patterns may be scale-sensitive, requiring controlled experiments\n      to disentangle scale from training duration.\"\n\n  - name: \"Statistical robustness framework\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-008\"\n    description: >\n      Bootstrap CI、多重比较校正、GDN exclusion sensitivity analysis、effect size 计算。\n    expected_results:\n      lambada_std_reduction_bootstrap_ci_pct: [22, 53]\n      lambada_rho_bootstrap_ci: [-0.78, -0.35]\n      lambada_rho_bootstrap_ci_crosses_zero: false\n      lambada_rho_gdn_excluded: -0.58\n      lambada_rho_gdn_excluded_p: 0.12\n      claims_surviving_gdn_exclusion: 0\n      bonferroni_significant_benchmarks: 0\n      fdr_significant_benchmarks: 1\n      cohens_d_lambada_convergence: 0.42\n      jaccard_bootstrap_ci: [0.03, 0.19]\n      jaccard_pairwise_mean: 0.09\n    result_rationale: >\n      Bootstrap 95% CI 极宽：std reduction [22%, 53%]（原 point estimate 79% 完全在 CI 外，\n      因为排除 GDN 后 point estimate 降至 38%），ρ CI [-0.78, -0.35] 不 cross zero 但包含了\n      远弱于原始 claim 的值。致命打击：GDN exclusion 后 ρ=-0.58, p=0.12——核心 convergence claim\n      依赖 GDN 数据点，而 GDN 有 D004 confound。Bonferroni 校正后零个 benchmark 显著（LAMBADA\n      raw p=0.12 × 6 benchmarks），FDR 下 LAMBADA 勉强 pass（q=0.12 < 0.15 的宽松阈值）。\n      Jaccard CI 上界达 0.19，原始 \"< 0.10\" claim 在 CI 内但 upper bound 接近 0.20，\n      paradox 程度大幅减弱。所有 core claims 在 GDN excluded 的 robustness check 下 fail。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 6: Bootstrap robustness analysis (10,000 iterations)\"\n        columns: [metric, point_estimate, ci_lower, ci_upper, gdn_excluded_estimate, interpretation]\n        rows:\n          - [lambada_std_reduction_pct, 38, 22, 53, 22, \"CI wide; GDN exclusion at lower bound\"]\n          - [lambada_spearman_rho, -0.58, -0.78, -0.35, -0.58, \"does not cross 0, but weak\"]\n          - [lambada_permutation_p, 0.117, \"-\", \"-\", 0.12, \"not significant at 0.05\"]\n          - [jaccard_pairwise_mean, 0.09, 0.03, 0.19, 0.11, \"upper CI approaches 0.20\"]\n          - [cohens_d_convergence, 0.42, 0.15, 0.68, 0.28, \"small-to-medium effect\"]\n      - title: \"Table 7: Multi-comparison correction across benchmarks\"\n        columns: [benchmark, raw_p, bonferroni_p, fdr_q, significant_bonferroni, significant_fdr_015]\n        rows:\n          - [LAMBADA, 0.117, 0.702, 0.117, \"No\", \"Yes (marginal)\"]\n          - [ARC-Easy, 0.350, 1.000, 0.420, \"No\", \"No\"]\n          - [ARC-Challenge, 0.680, 1.000, 0.680, \"No\", \"No\"]\n          - [HellaSwag, 0.920, 1.000, 0.920, \"No\", \"No\"]\n          - [WinoGrande, 0.610, 1.000, 0.680, \"No\", \"No\"]\n          - [MMLU, 0.480, 1.000, 0.576, \"No\", \"No\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 9: Bootstrap distribution of LAMBADA ρ，含/不含 GDN。含 GDN 分布集中在 -0.9 附近，排除后 shift 至 -0.58 附近且 variance 大增，大量 bootstrap sample 落在 [-0.5, -0.3] 区间。\"\n      - \"Fig 10: Forest plot of convergence effect sizes across 6 benchmarks with 95% bootstrap CI。只有 LAMBADA 的 CI 不 cross zero（但 effect size 小），其余均 cross。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Robustness analysis 是压垮原始 framing 的最后一根稻草。GDN confound 致命：排除后无 benchmark\n      达到 conventional significance。79% std reduction 是含 GDN 的 inflated estimate，真实值约 38%\n      CI [22-53%]。Jaccard upper CI 接近 0.20 削弱 paradox 强度。Reframed paper 必须诚实报告\n      这些 robustness results，但可以 flip narrative：正因为 aggregate convergence claim fragile，\n      才更需要 per-example methodology 来 reveal 真实行为——aggregate 的不可靠性本身就是论点。\n\n  - name: \"Wang et al. explicit differentiation\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-009\"\n    description: >\n      逐条对比 Wang et al. 的 convergence-related 报告与我们的分析。\n    expected_results:\n      wang_convergence_statements_found: 3\n      wang_qualitative_overlap_pct: 65\n      our_unique_contributions_surviving: 2\n      differentiation_strength: \"weak-to-moderate\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Wang et al. 的 qualitative convergence 观察覆盖了我们大部分 aggregate 发现。他们在 Section 4.2\n      明确提到 \"performance gaps narrow with increasing attention ratio\"（与 Claim 1 重叠），\n      在 Section 5.1 提到 \"effect is more pronounced at larger scale\"（与 Claim 2 重叠），\n      甚至在 supplementary 中有一个 per-model performance variance 图（虽未做 formal analysis）。\n      我们的 unique contribution 剩余：(a) per-example analysis revealing non-overlapping sample sets\n      (Jaccard metric)——但 robustness weakened，(b) methodology framework itself。Wang et al.\n      没做 per-example analysis 这一点是确定的，但他们的 qualitative coverage 意味着我们的\n      incremental contribution 主要是 methodological 而非 empirical。这恰好 align with reframe。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 8: Wang et al. vs our analysis — claim-by-claim overlap\"\n        columns: [claim_area, wang_coverage, our_original_claim, incremental_contribution, survives_robustness]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Aggregate convergence\", \"qualitative, Fig 4/7\", \"quantitative ρ, std trajectory\", \"marginal — their plots show same trend\", \"No (GDN confound)\"]\n          - [\"Scale dependency\", \"mentioned in discussion\", \"binary contrast 340M vs 1.3B\", \"weak — rebound unexplained\", \"No (training confound)\"]\n          - [\"Per-example mechanism\", \"not analyzed\", \"Jaccard, net-effect asymmetry\", \"unique — methodology contribution\", \"Partially (CI wide)\"]\n          - [\"Task specificity\", \"not analyzed\", \"retrieval demand spectrum\", \"collapsed — dose-response R²=0.28\", \"No\"]\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      与 Wang et al. 的 differentiation 确认 incremental contribution 不足以支撑 empirical discovery\n      paper。但 per-example methodology 是 genuine gap——他们有 model zoo 却没做 per-example analysis。\n      Reframed paper 的定位由此明确：我们的贡献是 methodology（per-example divergence metrics + analysis\n      framework），不是 empirical finding（equalizer effect）。Wang et al. model zoo 变成我们的\n      case study platform 而非竞争对手。\n\n  - name: \"Convergence-divergence bridge analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-010\"\n    description: >\n      绘制 aggregate convergence 与 per-example divergence metrics 随 attention ratio 的共演化曲线。\n    expected_results:\n      convergence_divergence_correlation: -0.45\n      convergence_divergence_p: 0.22\n      jaccard_vs_attention_ratio_trend: \"weakly decreasing (more attention → slightly lower Jaccard)\"\n      net_effect_asymmetry_vs_ratio: \"non-monotonic\"\n      paradox_strength: \"moderate but noisy\"\n      jaccard_pairwise_mean: 0.12\n    result_rationale: >\n      \"Paradox\" 的核心图表——aggregate convergence 上升但 per-example divergence 持续存在——在 GDN\n      excluded 数据上大幅减弱。Aggregate convergence 本身就弱（ρ=-0.58），per-example Jaccard 随\n      attention ratio 仅 weakly decreasing（而非原本期望的 \"stable low\"），意味着更多 attention 时\n      sample overlap 略有上升，部分 undermines \"non-overlapping mechanisms\" 叙事。\n      convergence-divergence correlation r=-0.45 方向对但 p=0.22 不显著（n=5 ratio points）。\n      Net-effect asymmetry 非单调进一步 complicates 图。Overall：\"paradox\" 仍 visible 但不 crisp，\n      更像 noisy tendency 而非 clean phenomenon。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 9: Convergence-divergence co-evolution by attention ratio (LAMBADA, 1.3B, GDN excluded)\"\n        columns: [attention_ratio, cross_arch_std, jaccard_mean, net_effect_asymmetry, n_helped_union, n_hurt_union]\n        rows:\n          - [h0, 0.024, \"-\", \"-\", \"-\", \"-\"]\n          - [h1, 0.021, 0.14, 0.32, 812, 743]\n          - [h3, 0.018, 0.11, 0.41, 924, 868]\n          - [h6, 0.016, 0.10, 0.28, 1051, 982]\n          - [h24, 0.015, 0.12, 0.35, 1103, 1044]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 11: Dual-axis plot。左轴 cross-arch std（蓝，下降趋势但 shallow），右轴 Jaccard mean（红，基本 flat 在 0.10-0.14 间轻微波动）。两条线没有形成 dramatic 的 'scissors' pattern，而是都比较 flat。Shaded area 为 bootstrap 95% CI——Jaccard 的 CI 极宽，包含 0.20。\"\n      - \"Fig 12: Net-effect asymmetry vs attention ratio，非单调（h3 处 peak），与 convergence 无 clean 关系。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Bridge analysis 产出一个 \"soft\" paradox 而非 \"crisp\" paradox。Aggregate convergence 弱，\n      per-example divergence 存在但 Jaccard 波动大。Reframed paper 处理：不再 claim \"paradox\" 作为\n      main finding，而是将 convergence-divergence gap 作为 per-example methodology 揭示的一个\n      illustrative example——\"even this modest aggregate convergence masks substantial per-example\n      heterogeneity, demonstrating why per-example analysis is necessary.\" Downgrade 从 core\n      contribution 到 motivating example。\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10818,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10818},"output_tokens":22,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9ac07f93-f2d8-47a3-aa19-d12650caf590","uuid":"a9a20d57-b33a-4f8c-9e74-a21840b9c730"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":184394,"duration_api_ms":185528,"num_turns":1,"result":"```yaml\ntier: worst\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  原始三条 claim 均无法以当前强度成立。Reframe 策略（仍冲 EMNLP，不降级）：放弃 \"equalizer effect\" 作为核心贡献，\n  转向 per-example analysis methodology paper。新 angle: \"Per-Example Probing Reveals Hidden Heterogeneity\n  in Hybrid Architecture Evaluations\"——核心论点变为：aggregate benchmark 评估掩盖了架构间的 per-example 行为差异，\n  即使 aggregate 指标相近，底层机制完全不同。这是 methodology + cautionary tale 的 framing：(1) 提出\n  per-example divergence metrics (Jaccard, net-effect asymmetry) 作为评估工具，(2) 用 Wang et al. model zoo\n  做 case study 展示 aggregate metric 的盲区，(3) 给出 practitioner recommendation——选架构时不能只看\n  leaderboard 数字。即使 equalizer effect 本身不 robust，per-example heterogeneity 的存在及其对架构选择的\n  implication 仍是 solid contribution。标题: \"Beyond Aggregate Benchmarks: Per-Example Analysis Exposes\n  Architecture-Specific Behavior in Hybrid Language Models\"。投 EMNLP Findings。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"Task-specificity characterization of equalizer effect\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-001\"\n    description: >\n      对 6 个 benchmark 计算各 attention ratio 下 cross-architecture std，构建连续 retrieval demand 谱。\n    expected_results:\n      lambada_rho: -0.60\n      lambada_rho_permutation_p: 0.117\n      lambada_std_reduction_pct: 38\n      arc_easy_rho: -0.30\n      arc_easy_p: 0.35\n      arc_challenge_rho: -0.10\n      hellaswag_rho: 0.05\n      winogrande_rho: 0.15\n      mmlu_rho: -0.20\n      benchmarks_with_rho_below_neg05: 1\n      dose_response_r_squared: 0.28\n    result_rationale: >\n      排除 GDN 后 LAMBADA ρ 从 -1.0 退化至约 -0.6（RetNet 和 HGRN2 的 h24 点 std 回弹导致非单调），\n      permutation p 跃升至 0.117 不再显著。核心原因：D004 confound——GDN 在高 attention ratio 配置下\n      使用了不同的 normalization scheme，其 std 被人为压低，移除后整体 convergence 幅度大打折扣。\n      ARC-Easy ρ 仅 -0.3，其余 benchmark 无趋势。连续 retrieval demand 谱的 R² 仅 0.28，\n      WinoGrande 作为含 retrieval 成分的 coreference task 却 ρ=+0.15，直接破坏 dose-response 叙事。\n      无法建立\"retrieval demand 调制 convergence strength\"的 principled taxonomy。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 1: Cross-architecture std reduction and Spearman ρ by benchmark (1.3B, GDN excluded)\"\n        columns: [benchmark, retrieval_demand_score, std_at_h0, std_at_h24, reduction_pct, spearman_rho, permutation_p]\n        rows:\n          - [LAMBADA, 0.90, 0.024, 0.015, 38, -0.60, 0.117]\n          - [ARC-Easy, 0.55, 0.031, 0.025, 19, -0.30, 0.350]\n          - [ARC-Challenge, 0.50, 0.028, 0.026, 7, -0.10, 0.680]\n          - [HellaSwag, 0.30, 0.019, 0.019, 0, 0.05, 0.920]\n          - [WinoGrande, 0.45, 0.022, 0.025, -14, 0.15, 0.610]\n          - [MMLU, 0.35, 0.035, 0.031, 11, -0.20, 0.480]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 1: 6-panel plot of cross-arch std vs attention ratio。LAMBADA 面板显示含/不含 GDN 两条线——含 GDN 时呈现漂亮的单调下降，排除 GDN 后 h24 处 rebound 明显，非单调。其余 5 个 benchmark 基本 flat 或 noisy。\"\n      - \"Fig 2: Dose-response scatter (retrieval demand score vs ρ)，6 点，R²=0.28，WinoGrande 为明显 outlier 位于右上方。虚线为线性 fit，95% CI 极宽。\"\n    analysis: >\n      task-specificity 叙事崩溃。GDN 排除后 LAMBADA 自身不再显著，dose-response 因 WinoGrande outlier\n      R² 仅 0.28。Claim 1 无法以\"retrieval demand 调制 convergence\"的形式成立。但 per-example 异质性\n      本身仍存在——reframe 方向：不再声称 convergence 是 systematic phenomenon，而是用这些负结果作为\n      evidence 说明 aggregate metric 不可靠。\n\n  - name: \"Multi-benchmark per-example analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-002\"\n    description: >\n      对 HellaSwag、ARC-Easy、ARC-Challenge 收集 1.3B 和 340M 的 per-example logprob 数据，\n      分析非 LAMBADA 任务的 per-example convergence 行为。\n    expected_results:\n      hellaswag_per_example_convergence: \"absent — random reshuffling\"\n      arc_easy_rho_per_example: -0.15\n      arc_easy_per_example_pattern: \"weak convergence in a ~12% subset, rest noise\"\n      arc_challenge_rho_per_example: 0.05\n      arc_challenge_per_example_pattern: \"no detectable structure\"\n      fraction_samples_with_consistent_direction: 0.18\n      cross_benchmark_jaccard_convergent_samples: 0.04\n    result_rationale: >\n      非 LAMBADA 任务本身 aggregate convergence 就不存在或极弱（exp-001 已示），per-example 分析\n      进一步暴露问题：ARC-Easy 的 per-example 分析反而显示大部分 sample 上 attention 的 effect 方向\n      在不同 architecture 间不一致，只有约 12% 的 easy retrieval-type 题目呈现弱 convergence，\n      但该 subset 太小无法支撑 claim。HellaSwag per-example 完全无结构——helped/hurt set 在不同\n      attention ratio 间剧烈变动，bootstrap stability <0.3。ARC-Challenge 类似。\n      这直接破坏了 \"task-specificity\" 叙事：原本期望非 LAMBADA 任务 per-example 也无 convergence\n      （从而 confirm aggregate 结果），但实际是 per-example 呈现 weak, inconsistent convergence 信号，\n      既无法说 \"converging\" 也无法干净地说 \"not converging\"，而是 noisy mess，削弱了\n      LAMBADA 作为 clean contrast 的地位。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 2: Per-example convergence metrics across benchmarks (1.3B)\"\n        columns: [benchmark, n_samples, frac_consistent_direction, per_example_rho, bootstrap_stability, interpretation]\n        rows:\n          - [LAMBADA, 5153, 0.61, -0.55, 0.78, \"moderate convergence (weakened vs aggregate)\"]\n          - [ARC-Easy, 2376, 0.23, -0.15, 0.41, \"weak, noisy — small convergent subset\"]\n          - [ARC-Challenge, 1172, 0.15, 0.05, 0.22, \"no structure\"]\n          - [HellaSwag, 10042, 0.12, 0.02, 0.18, \"no structure — random reshuffling\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 3: Per-example effect heatmap (sample × attention ratio) for 4 benchmarks。LAMBADA 显示一定的 block structure（某些 sample 一致 helped/hurt），但 block 边界模糊。ARC-Easy 有零星 cluster。HellaSwag 和 ARC-Challenge 基本纯噪声。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Per-example 分析未能干净地 validate task-specificity。LAMBADA per-example ρ 从 aggregate 的 -0.6\n      进一步弱化至 -0.55（因为 per-example level 噪声更大），而非 LAMBADA 任务并非 \"cleanly absent\"\n      而是 \"noisy and inconclusive\"。这意味着无法构建 \"LAMBADA converges, others don't\" 的 clean binary。\n      但 per-example heterogeneity 本身（不同 architecture 在相同 sample 上行为不同）在所有 benchmark\n      上都存在——这支持 reframed methodology paper 的核心论点。\n\n  - name: \"Helped/hurt sample characterization\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-003\"\n    description: >\n      对 LAMBADA 的 helped/hurt sample 计算 token frequency、context length、perplexity、\n      topic distribution，测试是否有可解释的 feature 区分。\n    expected_results:\n      best_feature_p_value: 0.034\n      best_feature_name: \"target_token_log_frequency\"\n      best_feature_effect_size_cohens_d: 0.18\n      context_length_p: 0.22\n      perplexity_p: 0.41\n      topic_chi2_p: 0.15\n      cross_architecture_feature_difference: \"not significant after Bonferroni\"\n      sample_feature_best_p: 0.034\n    result_rationale: >\n      无 feature 通过 Bonferroni 校正后的 p<0.01 阈值。最佳 single feature (target token frequency)\n      raw p=0.034 但校正后 p≈0.14（4 features × 3 architectures = 12 comparisons）。\n      effect size Cohen's d=0.18 极小。核心问题：helped/hurt sample 的区分不在简单的 surface feature 上，\n      而可能在更高阶的 distributional property 中，但我们没有足够的 feature engineering 来捕捉。\n      Cross-architecture comparison 更惨：三个 architecture 的 helped sample 在所有 feature 上的\n      分布无显著差异，意味着无法给出 \"GDN helps long-context samples while HGRN2 helps rare-token samples\"\n      这类 interpretable story。Claim 3 的 mechanistic depth 严重不足。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 3: Feature comparison of helped vs hurt samples on LAMBADA (per architecture)\"\n        columns: [feature, architecture, helped_mean, hurt_mean, cohens_d, raw_p, bonferroni_p]\n        rows:\n          - [target_token_log_freq, GDN, 8.21, 8.45, 0.18, 0.034, 0.41]\n          - [target_token_log_freq, RetNet, 8.18, 8.39, 0.15, 0.065, 0.78]\n          - [target_token_log_freq, HGRN2, 8.30, 8.42, 0.09, 0.210, 1.00]\n          - [context_length, GDN, 42.3, 40.8, 0.08, 0.220, 1.00]\n          - [context_length, RetNet, 43.1, 41.5, 0.10, 0.180, 1.00]\n          - [context_length, HGRN2, 41.8, 41.2, 0.04, 0.550, 1.00]\n          - [baseline_perplexity, GDN, 12.4, 11.8, 0.07, 0.410, 1.00]\n          - [baseline_perplexity, RetNet, 13.1, 12.5, 0.06, 0.480, 1.00]\n          - [baseline_perplexity, HGRN2, 12.0, 11.9, 0.01, 0.870, 1.00]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 4: Violin plot of target token log-frequency for helped vs hurt samples，三个 architecture 分 panel。分布高度重叠，几乎不可区分。\"\n      - \"Fig 5: 2D t-SNE of sample feature vectors，colored by helped/hurt。无可见 cluster 分离。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Sample characterization 失败——无可解释结构。这对原始 Claim 3 是致命的：我们说 \"attention acts on\n      different samples per architecture\" 但无法解释 why。对 reframed paper 影响较小：methodology paper\n      可以将此作为 open question (\"per-example heterogeneity exists but its drivers remain unclear,\n      motivating future work on finer-grained sample characterization\")。\n\n  - name: \"Attention weight extraction and visualization\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-004\"\n    description: >\n      提取 h3-1 配置下三个 architecture 的 attention weight pattern，分析与 per-example effect 的相关性。\n    expected_results:\n      attention_per_example_correlation_gdn: 0.11\n      attention_per_example_correlation_retnet: 0.08\n      attention_per_example_correlation_hgrn2: 0.14\n      attention_per_example_correlation_mean: 0.11\n      cross_arch_attention_similarity: 0.35\n      attention_entropy_helped_vs_hurt_p: 0.18\n    result_rationale: >\n      Attention pattern 与 per-example effect 的相关性极低（mean r=0.11，远低于 pass criterion 0.3）。\n      原因：h3-1 配置中 attention 只有 1 层（共 24 层中），大量信息处理发生在 recurrence layers 中，\n      单层 attention 的 weight pattern 不足以解释 per-example 行为差异。attention entropy 在\n      helped vs hurt samples 间也无显著差异（p=0.18）。cross-architecture attention similarity 0.35\n      表明不同 architecture 的 attention layer 确实关注不同 position，但这与 per-example outcome 无法\n      建立因果链。没有 mechanistic story。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 4: Attention pattern analysis (h3-1, 1.3B)\"\n        columns: [architecture, attn_per_example_corr, attn_entropy_mean, entropy_helped_vs_hurt_p, cross_arch_cosine_sim]\n        rows:\n          - [GDN, 0.11, 3.42, 0.22, \"-\"]\n          - [RetNet, 0.08, 3.18, 0.31, \"0.35 (vs GDN)\"]\n          - [HGRN2, 0.14, 3.55, 0.14, \"0.32 (vs GDN)\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 6: Attention heatmap for 10 representative LAMBADA samples across 3 architectures。视觉上 pattern 不同（GDN 集中在末尾 token，RetNet 更 distributed，HGRN2 有双峰），但这些差异与 helped/hurt 无对应关系。\"\n      - \"Fig 7: Scatter of attention-based prediction score vs actual per-example effect。三个 panel 均为散点云，r<0.15。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Mechanistic analysis 失败。无法从 attention weights 解释 per-example divergence。这对 Claim 3\n      \"complementary mechanisms\" 是毁灭性的——我们无法说明 mechanisms 是什么。对 reframed paper：\n      methodology paper 不需要 explain 机制，只需 demonstrate 现象存在。attention 可视化仍可作为\n      qualitative illustration 放在 appendix，但不再是 core evidence。\n\n  - name: \"Architecture expansion check\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-005\"\n    description: >\n      搜索 Wang et al. model zoo 及其他来源，寻找 GDN/RetNet/HGRN2 之外的 hybrid architectures。\n    expected_results:\n      additional_architectures_found: 0\n      wang_et_al_architectures_total: 3\n      mamba_hybrid_available: false\n      rwkv_hybrid_available: false\n      architectures_tested: 3\n    result_rationale: >\n      Wang et al. (2507.06457) 的 model zoo 明确仅包含 GDN、RetNet、HGRN2 三种 architecture。\n      搜索 HuggingFace 和其他公开 model zoo 后未发现使用相同 training setup（相同数据、相同 token 数、\n      相同超参搜索）的其他 hybrid architecture checkpoint。Mamba-2 hybrid 存在于 Zamba 等项目中但\n      training setup 完全不同，apple-to-apple comparison 不可能。n=3 limitation 无法缓解。\n      这对原始 Claim 1 的 generalizability 和 reframed paper 都是问题——reviewer 会质疑\n      findings 是否只是这 3 个特定 architecture 的 artifact。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Architecture expansion 失败，n=3 limitation 确认。Reframed paper 需要在 Limitations 中\n      prominently 承认，并 argue 3 architectures 代表 3 种不同 recurrence mechanism（这是 Wang et al.\n      的选择 rationale），同时将 generalization 作为 future work。\n\n  - name: \"340M rebound mechanism analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-007\"\n    description: >\n      深入分析 340M 在 attn=8 处的非单调 rebound，对比 1.3B 同 attention ratio 的 per-example 行为。\n    expected_results:\n      rebound_mechanism_identified: false\n      scale_340m_rebound_magnitude: 0.018\n      scale_1_3b_at_same_ratio_std: 0.007\n      per_example_overlap_340m_1_3b: 0.22\n      training_tokens_confound_resolved: false\n      explanation_confidence: \"low\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      340M rebound 无法解释。Per-example 对比显示 340M 和 1.3B 在 attn=8 ratio 上 affected sample\n      overlap 仅 0.22（低但非零），暗示 scale 和 attention 以不可分离的方式交互。更严重的是，\n      340M 训练了 20B tokens vs 1.3B 训练了 100B tokens（Wang et al. setup），training token count\n      与 model scale 完全 confounded，无法归因 rebound 到 \"insufficient model capacity\" vs\n      \"insufficient training\"。这使 Claim 2 退化为纯粹的 unexplained observation：我们看到\n      340M 和 1.3B 行为不同，但无法说 why。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 5: 340M vs 1.3B per-example comparison at attn=8\"\n        columns: [metric, \"340M\", \"1.3B\", delta]\n        rows:\n          - [cross_arch_std, 0.018, 0.007, \"+0.011\"]\n          - [per_example_overlap_jaccard, \"-\", \"-\", 0.22]\n          - [rebound_samples_frac, 0.31, 0.08, \"+0.23\"]\n          - [training_tokens_B, 20, 100, \"confounded\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 8: 340M vs 1.3B cross-arch std trajectory。1.3B 单调下降（GDN excluded 后变为 weakly 下降），340M 在 h8 处 rebound。两条线 diverge 但 error bars 在 h8 处 overlap。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Claim 2 (scale-dependent convergence) 退化为 unexplained observation。Training token confound\n      无法解开。Reframed paper 处理方式：将 scale contrast 作为一个 observation 报告（不作为 claim），\n      在 Discussion 中 acknowledge training token confound，frame as \"preliminary evidence that\n      per-example heterogeneity patterns may be scale-sensitive, requiring controlled experiments\n      to disentangle scale from training duration.\"\n\n  - name: \"Statistical robustness framework\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-008\"\n    description: >\n      Bootstrap CI、多重比较校正、GDN exclusion sensitivity analysis、effect size 计算。\n    expected_results:\n      lambada_std_reduction_bootstrap_ci_pct: [22, 53]\n      lambada_rho_bootstrap_ci: [-0.78, -0.35]\n      lambada_rho_bootstrap_ci_crosses_zero: false\n      lambada_rho_gdn_excluded: -0.58\n      lambada_rho_gdn_excluded_p: 0.12\n      claims_surviving_gdn_exclusion: 0\n      bonferroni_significant_benchmarks: 0\n      fdr_significant_benchmarks: 1\n      cohens_d_lambada_convergence: 0.42\n      jaccard_bootstrap_ci: [0.03, 0.19]\n      jaccard_pairwise_mean: 0.09\n    result_rationale: >\n      Bootstrap 95% CI 极宽：std reduction [22%, 53%]（原 point estimate 79% 完全在 CI 外，\n      因为排除 GDN 后 point estimate 降至 38%），ρ CI [-0.78, -0.35] 不 cross zero 但包含了\n      远弱于原始 claim 的值。致命打击：GDN exclusion 后 ρ=-0.58, p=0.12——核心 convergence claim\n      依赖 GDN 数据点，而 GDN 有 D004 confound。Bonferroni 校正后零个 benchmark 显著（LAMBADA\n      raw p=0.12 × 6 benchmarks），FDR 下 LAMBADA 勉强 pass（q=0.12 < 0.15 的宽松阈值）。\n      Jaccard CI 上界达 0.19，原始 \"< 0.10\" claim 在 CI 内但 upper bound 接近 0.20，\n      paradox 程度大幅减弱。所有 core claims 在 GDN excluded 的 robustness check 下 fail。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 6: Bootstrap robustness analysis (10,000 iterations)\"\n        columns: [metric, point_estimate, ci_lower, ci_upper, gdn_excluded_estimate, interpretation]\n        rows:\n          - [lambada_std_reduction_pct, 38, 22, 53, 22, \"CI wide; GDN exclusion at lower bound\"]\n          - [lambada_spearman_rho, -0.58, -0.78, -0.35, -0.58, \"does not cross 0, but weak\"]\n          - [lambada_permutation_p, 0.117, \"-\", \"-\", 0.12, \"not significant at 0.05\"]\n          - [jaccard_pairwise_mean, 0.09, 0.03, 0.19, 0.11, \"upper CI approaches 0.20\"]\n          - [cohens_d_convergence, 0.42, 0.15, 0.68, 0.28, \"small-to-medium effect\"]\n      - title: \"Table 7: Multi-comparison correction across benchmarks\"\n        columns: [benchmark, raw_p, bonferroni_p, fdr_q, significant_bonferroni, significant_fdr_015]\n        rows:\n          - [LAMBADA, 0.117, 0.702, 0.117, \"No\", \"Yes (marginal)\"]\n          - [ARC-Easy, 0.350, 1.000, 0.420, \"No\", \"No\"]\n          - [ARC-Challenge, 0.680, 1.000, 0.680, \"No\", \"No\"]\n          - [HellaSwag, 0.920, 1.000, 0.920, \"No\", \"No\"]\n          - [WinoGrande, 0.610, 1.000, 0.680, \"No\", \"No\"]\n          - [MMLU, 0.480, 1.000, 0.576, \"No\", \"No\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 9: Bootstrap distribution of LAMBADA ρ，含/不含 GDN。含 GDN 分布集中在 -0.9 附近，排除后 shift 至 -0.58 附近且 variance 大增，大量 bootstrap sample 落在 [-0.5, -0.3] 区间。\"\n      - \"Fig 10: Forest plot of convergence effect sizes across 6 benchmarks with 95% bootstrap CI。只有 LAMBADA 的 CI 不 cross zero（但 effect size 小），其余均 cross。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Robustness analysis 是压垮原始 framing 的最后一根稻草。GDN confound 致命：排除后无 benchmark\n      达到 conventional significance。79% std reduction 是含 GDN 的 inflated estimate，真实值约 38%\n      CI [22-53%]。Jaccard upper CI 接近 0.20 削弱 paradox 强度。Reframed paper 必须诚实报告\n      这些 robustness results，但可以 flip narrative：正因为 aggregate convergence claim fragile，\n      才更需要 per-example methodology 来 reveal 真实行为——aggregate 的不可靠性本身就是论点。\n\n  - name: \"Wang et al. explicit differentiation\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-009\"\n    description: >\n      逐条对比 Wang et al. 的 convergence-related 报告与我们的分析。\n    expected_results:\n      wang_convergence_statements_found: 3\n      wang_qualitative_overlap_pct: 65\n      our_unique_contributions_surviving: 2\n      differentiation_strength: \"weak-to-moderate\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Wang et al. 的 qualitative convergence 观察覆盖了我们大部分 aggregate 发现。他们在 Section 4.2\n      明确提到 \"performance gaps narrow with increasing attention ratio\"（与 Claim 1 重叠），\n      在 Section 5.1 提到 \"effect is more pronounced at larger scale\"（与 Claim 2 重叠），\n      甚至在 supplementary 中有一个 per-model performance variance 图（虽未做 formal analysis）。\n      我们的 unique contribution 剩余：(a) per-example analysis revealing non-overlapping sample sets\n      (Jaccard metric)——但 robustness weakened，(b) methodology framework itself。Wang et al.\n      没做 per-example analysis 这一点是确定的，但他们的 qualitative coverage 意味着我们的\n      incremental contribution 主要是 methodological 而非 empirical。这恰好 align with reframe。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 8: Wang et al. vs our analysis — claim-by-claim overlap\"\n        columns: [claim_area, wang_coverage, our_original_claim, incremental_contribution, survives_robustness]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Aggregate convergence\", \"qualitative, Fig 4/7\", \"quantitative ρ, std trajectory\", \"marginal — their plots show same trend\", \"No (GDN confound)\"]\n          - [\"Scale dependency\", \"mentioned in discussion\", \"binary contrast 340M vs 1.3B\", \"weak — rebound unexplained\", \"No (training confound)\"]\n          - [\"Per-example mechanism\", \"not analyzed\", \"Jaccard, net-effect asymmetry\", \"unique — methodology contribution\", \"Partially (CI wide)\"]\n          - [\"Task specificity\", \"not analyzed\", \"retrieval demand spectrum\", \"collapsed — dose-response R²=0.28\", \"No\"]\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      与 Wang et al. 的 differentiation 确认 incremental contribution 不足以支撑 empirical discovery\n      paper。但 per-example methodology 是 genuine gap——他们有 model zoo 却没做 per-example analysis。\n      Reframed paper 的定位由此明确：我们的贡献是 methodology（per-example divergence metrics + analysis\n      framework），不是 empirical finding（equalizer effect）。Wang et al. model zoo 变成我们的\n      case study platform 而非竞争对手。\n\n  - name: \"Convergence-divergence bridge analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-010\"\n    description: >\n      绘制 aggregate convergence 与 per-example divergence metrics 随 attention ratio 的共演化曲线。\n    expected_results:\n      convergence_divergence_correlation: -0.45\n      convergence_divergence_p: 0.22\n      jaccard_vs_attention_ratio_trend: \"weakly decreasing (more attention → slightly lower Jaccard)\"\n      net_effect_asymmetry_vs_ratio: \"non-monotonic\"\n      paradox_strength: \"moderate but noisy\"\n      jaccard_pairwise_mean: 0.12\n    result_rationale: >\n      \"Paradox\" 的核心图表——aggregate convergence 上升但 per-example divergence 持续存在——在 GDN\n      excluded 数据上大幅减弱。Aggregate convergence 本身就弱（ρ=-0.58），per-example Jaccard 随\n      attention ratio 仅 weakly decreasing（而非原本期望的 \"stable low\"），意味着更多 attention 时\n      sample overlap 略有上升，部分 undermines \"non-overlapping mechanisms\" 叙事。\n      convergence-divergence correlation r=-0.45 方向对但 p=0.22 不显著（n=5 ratio points）。\n      Net-effect asymmetry 非单调进一步 complicates 图。Overall：\"paradox\" 仍 visible 但不 crisp，\n      更像 noisy tendency 而非 clean phenomenon。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 9: Convergence-divergence co-evolution by attention ratio (LAMBADA, 1.3B, GDN excluded)\"\n        columns: [attention_ratio, cross_arch_std, jaccard_mean, net_effect_asymmetry, n_helped_union, n_hurt_union]\n        rows:\n          - [h0, 0.024, \"-\", \"-\", \"-\", \"-\"]\n          - [h1, 0.021, 0.14, 0.32, 812, 743]\n          - [h3, 0.018, 0.11, 0.41, 924, 868]\n          - [h6, 0.016, 0.10, 0.28, 1051, 982]\n          - [h24, 0.015, 0.12, 0.35, 1103, 1044]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 11: Dual-axis plot。左轴 cross-arch std（蓝，下降趋势但 shallow），右轴 Jaccard mean（红，基本 flat 在 0.10-0.14 间轻微波动）。两条线没有形成 dramatic 的 'scissors' pattern，而是都比较 flat。Shaded area 为 bootstrap 95% CI——Jaccard 的 CI 极宽，包含 0.20。\"\n      - \"Fig 12: Net-effect asymmetry vs attention ratio，非单调（h3 处 peak），与 convergence 无 clean 关系。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Bridge analysis 产出一个 \"soft\" paradox 而非 \"crisp\" paradox。Aggregate convergence 弱，\n      per-example divergence 存在但 Jaccard 波动大。Reframed paper 处理：不再 claim \"paradox\" 作为\n      main finding，而是将 convergence-divergence gap 作为 per-example methodology 揭示的一个\n      illustrative example——\"even this modest aggregate convergence masks substantial per-example\n      heterogeneity, demonstrating why per-example analysis is necessary.\" Downgrade 从 core\n      contribution 到 motivating example。\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"9ac07f93-f2d8-47a3-aa19-d12650caf590","total_cost_usd":0.309241,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10818,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"output_tokens":9193,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10818,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":9193,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10818,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10818},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":5778,"outputTokens":19,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.005873,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":9193,"cacheReadInputTokens":11841,"cacheCreationInputTokens":10818,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.30336799999999997,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"d6e4644b-cf58-411f-9a75-69361c59c624"}
